    [
     1,
     "Hello,<div><br></div><div>I am wondering if the order of groups in a \r\n\r\n<span style=\"font-weight:400;font-style:normal\"><span><span>contrast matrix matters. To test it, I have generated the two attached ones and passed them through the following lines of code.</span></span></span></div><div><span style=\"font-weight:400;font-style:normal\"><span><span><br></span></span></span></div><div><span style=\"font-weight:400;font-style:normal\"><span><span>contrast_matrix &lt;- as.data.frame(fread(&#39;./Data/test1.tsv&#39;))<br>rownames(contrast_matrix) &lt;- contrast_matrix$Name<br>contrast_matrix$Name &lt;- NULL<br>contrast_matrix[<a href=\"http://is.na\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://is.na&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793231095379000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3JftkxPM5s8DcVXRuwIiBg\">is.na</a>(contrast_matrix)] &lt;- 0<br>contrast_matrix &lt;- as.matrix(contrast_matrix)</span></span></span></div><div><span style=\"font-weight:400;font-style:normal\"><span><span><br></span></span></span></div><div><span style=\"font-weight:400;font-style:normal\"><span><span>And then tried &quot;groupComparison&quot; on the same dataset using these two \r\n<span style=\"font-weight:400;font-style:normal\"><span><span>contrast matrices. Do you expect any difference in terms of the results? And this is the order of the groups in the dataset - the same as &quot;test2.tsv&quot;.</span></span></span></span></span></span></div><div><span style=\"font-weight:400;font-style:normal\"><span><span><span style=\"font-weight:400;font-style:normal\"><span><span><br></span></span></span></span></span></span></div><div><span style=\"font-weight:400;font-style:normal\"><span><span><span style=\"font-weight:400;font-style:normal\"><span><span>\r\n\r\n<span style=\"font-weight:400;font-style:normal\"><span><span>levels(df.MSstats.proc.Imputed$FeatureLevelData$GROUP)</span><span><br></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></div><div><span style=\"font-weight:400;font-style:normal\"><span><span><span style=\"font-weight:400;font-style:normal\"><span><span><span style=\"font-weight:400;font-style:normal\"><span><span>[1] &quot;D0_RPMI&quot;     &quot;D0_RPMI_t1&quot;  &quot;D1_BG_r1&quot;    &quot;D1_LPS_r1&quot;   &quot;D1_LPS_t1&quot;   &quot;D1_MDP_r1&quot;   &quot;D1_RPMI_r1&quot;  &quot;D1_RPMI_t1&quot;</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></div><div><span style=\"font-weight:400;font-style:normal\"><span><span><span style=\"font-weight:400;font-style:normal\"><span><span><span style=\"font-weight:400;font-style:normal\"><span><span>[9] &quot;D1_UA_r1&quot;    &quot;D1_UA_t1&quot;    &quot;D1_oxLDL_r1&quot; &quot;D1_oxLDL_t1&quot; &quot;D6_BG_r1&quot;    &quot;D6_LPS_r1&quot;   &quot;D6_MDP_r1&quot;   &quot;D6_MDP_t1&quot;</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></div><div><span style=\"font-weight:400;font-style:normal\"><span><span><span style=\"font-weight:400;font-style:normal\"><span><span><span style=\"font-weight:400;font-style:normal\"><span><span>[17] &quot;D6_RPMI_r1&quot;  &quot;D6_UA_r1&quot;    &quot;D6_oxLDL_r1&quot; &quot;D7_BG_r1&quot;    &quot;D7_LPS_r1&quot;   &quot;D7_MDP_r1&quot;   &quot;D7_RPMI_r1&quot;  &quot;D7_UA_r1&quot;</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></div><div><span style=\"font-weight:400;font-style:normal\"><span><span><span style=\"font-weight:400;font-style:normal\"><span><span><span style=\"font-weight:400;font-style:normal\"><span><span>[25] &quot;D7_oxLDL_r1&quot;</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></div><div><span style=\"font-weight:400;font-style:normal\"><span><span><span style=\"font-weight:400;font-style:normal\"><span><span><span style=\"font-weight:400;font-style:normal\"><span><span><br></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></div><div><span style=\"font-weight:400;font-style:normal\"><span><span><span style=\"font-weight:400;font-style:normal\"><span><span><span style=\"font-weight:400;font-style:normal\"><span><span>What I see is that for the common significantly regulated proteins (2384), the results (logfc and pval) are the same. But &quot;\r\n<span style=\"font-weight:400;font-style:normal\"><span><span>test1.tsv</span></span></span>&quot; reults in more regulated proteins (3420) when compared to &quot;<span style=\"font-weight:400;font-style:normal\"><span><span>test2.tsv</span></span></span>&quot; (2539) for all three comparisons combined. How do you explain this?<br></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></div><div><span style=\"font-weight:400;font-style:normal\"><span><span><span style=\"font-weight:400;font-style:normal\"><span><span><span style=\"font-weight:400;font-style:normal\"><span><span><br></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></div><div><span style=\"font-weight:400;font-style:normal\"><span><span><span style=\"font-weight:400;font-style:normal\"><span><span><span style=\"font-weight:400;font-style:normal\"><span><span>Best,</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></div><div><span style=\"font-weight:400;font-style:normal\"><span><span><span style=\"font-weight:400;font-style:normal\"><span><span><span style=\"font-weight:400;font-style:normal\"><span><span>Amir</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></div><div><span style=\"font-weight:400;font-style:normal\"><span><span><span style=\"font-weight:400;font-style:normal\"><span><span><span style=\"font-weight:400;font-style:normal\"><span><span><br></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></div>"
